1. Which of the following are disadvantages of using inheritance to provide Duck behavior?
    A. Code is duplicated across subclasses
        - duplication emerges as overrides spread
    B. Runtime behavior changes are difficult
        - behavior is fixed at compile time
    D. It's hard to gain knowledge of all duck behaviors
        - behavior knowledge becomes fragmented
    F. Changes can unintentionally affect other ducks
        - changes ripple unintentionally

2. Lots of things can drive change. List some reasons you've had to change code in your applications.
    - Unforeseen requirements emerged during the development process (both functional and nonfunctional)
    - My initial implementations didn't emphasize low coupling and high cohesion and therefore needed refactoring
    - 3rd party libraries changed resulting in changes in my code
    - My professor decided that the original implementation didn't match what he had envisioned for the product